s=slide('The package journey','Explain the overall system before demonstrating individual pages. Check-in creates the record; claim assigns a driver/cart; transit milestones must occur in sequence; recipient sign-off records receipt after Delivered. CE-20261004 is a fictional tracking number used consistently in the screenshots. Sources: Package model and UI controller.')
heading(s,'How a package moves through the system')
text(s,'Received at hub  →  Claimed by a driver',.8,2.2,11.8,.9,30,PURPLE,True,0)
text(s,'Loaded  →  En Route  →  Delivered',.8,3.6,11.8,.9,32,PURPLE,True,0)
text(s,'Recipient confirms receipt',.8,5.0,11.8,.9,30,PURPLE,True,0)
text(s,'A tracking number connects every step. Example: CE-20261004.',.8,6.45,11.8,.55,22,'666666',False,0)

s=slide('Hub Operator portal','The operator form records a tracking barcode/campus number, weight in pounds, dimensions in inches, campus destination, and optional urgent priority. HTML native constraints validate inputs; JavaScript rejects duplicate IDs. Successful submission creates a shared Package record and updates the tracking log without a full page reload. Screenshot: actual filled operator form. Source: pages/operator.html, js/app.js and js/models.js.')
heading(s,'Hub Operator: receive and record','WHAT WE BUILT')
